---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Stage from '../components/Stage.astro'
import { site } from '../site'

const description = 'John DeLong on faith, family, engineering leadership, and the things he builds on the side.'
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <section class="wrap section" style="padding-top: 88px">
    <div class="cols center">
      <div class="s7 stack" style="--gap: 24px">
        <h1 class="h1 in">Hi, I'm <em>{site.author}.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede in" style="--i: 1; font-size: 21px">
          I'm a Christian, a husband, and a dad to three girls. I lead a software team for work,
          and in my spare time I'm usually building something.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="s5 portrait-stage">
        <Stage aspectRatio={3 / 2}>
          <img src="/john-delong.webp" alt={`Portrait of ${site.author}`} width="1200" height="800" />
        </Stage>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">Faith and family</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          My Christian faith is the foundation I build my life around. I believe the Bible is God's Word,
          and I want it to shape how I love my family, how I lead, and how I treat the people around me.
        </p>
        <p>
          I want to make time for God and help our girls grow in their own faith. I also want them to know
          they can come to me about anything. I hope to be someone they still want to talk to and ask for
          advice when they're grown.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">Work</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          I grew up in Cedar Springs, Michigan, and studied computer engineering at Grand Valley State
          University. I started my career at Dematic, working on software for logistics sites.
        </p>
        <h3>Michigan Software Labs</h3>
        <p>
          I spent eleven years at Michigan Software Labs. I started as a developer, took on technical
          leadership for client projects, and eventually helped lead our development practice. Native
          iOS was my specialty. I helped teams modernize older apps and set patterns they could build on.
          I also led architecture decisions for web and cloud projects, worked with clients and designers to
          decide what to build next, and helped automate releases so we could ship changes with more confidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          As a practice lead, I stayed hands-on and worked with the other leads to establish shared
          engineering practices and code quality standards. I led technical interviews, mentored
          developers in regular 1:1s, and worked on making career paths clearer so people could see what
          growth looked like in their day-to-day work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over those eleven years, I helped build software for clients in logistics, healthcare, higher
          education, and other fields. A couple of projects stand out when I look back.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>LandstarOne.</strong> I built LandstarOne from the ground up and spent about seven years
          shipping releases, adding features, and shaping its architecture as the app grew. It reached
          about 16,000 monthly active users across iOS and Android, giving drivers a way to find and book
          loads from the road. I also led the iOS move to SwiftUI to improve accessibility and support
          larger text across the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Altus Virtual Care.</strong> I designed the AWS architecture and built the first version
          of a web app that connects hospital patients with doctors and family. Over about a year, I built
          out video calls, remote camera controls, and an Epic integration. I helped launch the product
          and handed it over to the Altus team so they could keep building on it.
        </p>
        <h3>National Heritage Academies</h3>
        <p>
          I now lead the school applications engineering team at National Heritage Academies. We build
          software that schools use to manage student information. I like staying close to the technical
          work, and I try to lead by listening first, clearing roadblocks, and giving people room to do good work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="cols">
      <h2 class="h2 s4 rvl">On the side</h2>
      <div class="prose s7 end rv">
        <p>
          In my spare time I like building software, taking photos, making videos, and working on the house.
          I've wired entire homes, installed a kitchen, insulated a house, remodeled bathrooms and a basement,
          and built a deck and floating shelves, to name a few projects. I also design and 3D-print things,
          including RC planes I get to fly, and I like trying to get better at latte art.
        </p>
        <p>
          Sidelong means from the side. It fits the things I make on the side and the fun of coming at a
          problem from a slightly different angle.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .portrait-stage img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
</style>
